 r←Test_ClientConfig_123(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;settings;tempDir;rc;msg
⍝ Ask "Exist" for an empty URI, and for one that carries a colon but no port number. Neither
⍝ names a Registry, so the answer is 0. It used to be a LENGTH ERROR, because the port came out
⍝ empty and was then compared with the ports of all defined Registries.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 tempDir←∆GetTempDir''
 F.DeleteFile tempDir,'/',TC.UserSettings.cfg_name   ⍝ Precaution
 settings←∆NewUserSettings(,⊂tempDir)                ⍝ Comes with two Registries defined
 →T.GoToTidyUp 2>≢settings.registries                ⍝ One would not be enough for a LENGTH ERROR

 →T.GoToTidyUp∨/settings.Exist¨'' 'https://localhost:/'

⍝ What is defined must still be found, by URI as well as by alias
 →T.GoToTidyUp~settings.Exist(⊃settings.registries).uri
 →T.GoToTidyUp~settings.Exist'[tatin]'

 r←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←F.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
